hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1109","Yaqoub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr ibn al-Hakam, and Yahya ibn Hakim told us: Yahya told us, and he is Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Ata’ told me, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Umair, on the authority of Aisha, “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him,” was not “It is more difficult to perform any of the voluntary rak’ahs than to perform the two rak’ahs before dawn.” Yahya bin Hakim said, “Ubayd bin Umair informed me."
